---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { GITHUB_REPO_URL } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Community"
  description="How to contribute to OELTKit — component proposals as the on-ramp — plus governance, the public roadmap, and the vendor-neutrality commitment."
  path="/community/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Community</span>
      <h1>Built in the open, useful to everyone</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        OELTKit is Apache 2.0 and developed in public. The fastest way to shape it is to tell us
        what component your courses are missing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--rule" id="contribute">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Contribute</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Component proposals are the on-ramp.</strong> You don't need to write code to make
        OELTKit better — describe an interaction you keep building by hand (the markup you wish an
        LLM could write, how a keyboard user should drive it, what it should report to the LMS) and
        open it as a proposal. Specs that start from real course needs become the best components.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO_URL}/issues`}>Open a component proposal or bug report</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Contributing guide</a> — code,
          docs, and testing contributions all welcome
        </li>
        <li>
          Accessibility reviews are first-class contributions: if you use assistive technology and
          something doesn't work, that's a priority issue.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--rule" id="governance">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Governance</h2>
      <p>
        OELTKit is maintainer-governed during the beta, with decisions made in public issues and
        ADRs in the main repo. As the contributor base grows, governance formalizes — the
        commitment that doesn't change is below.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Vendor neutrality:</strong> OELTKit is incubated by
        <a href="https://www.bcltraining.com">BCL Training</a>, and it stays useful to people who
        never become BCL clients. No feature is held back for a paid tier, no LMS or AI vendor gets
        preferential treatment, and the standards targets are decided by what practitioners need —
        not by anyone's product roadmap.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--rule" id="roadmap">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Roadmap</h2>
      <p>
        The roadmap lives on GitHub where you can comment on it, not in a slide deck:
        <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO_URL}/projects`}>OELTKit project board</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="funding-note">
        Sponsorship via Open Collective is planned; the link will appear here when the collective
        is live — not before.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--oelt-text-lg);
    color: var(--oelt-color-ink-soft);
  }

  .funding-note {
    color: var(--oelt-color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--oelt-text-sm);
  }
</style>
